<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Does Neuron Writer include AI content writing?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">No, Neuron Writer focuses specifically on content optimization and planning rather than AI content generation. It provides detailed recommendations on what to write about and how to optimize it, but you write the content yourself. This focus allows it to excel at optimization while keeping costs lower than all-in-one platforms.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How accurate is the content scoring?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Neuron Writer's content scoring is highly accurate and based on advanced NLP analysis of top-ranking content. It considers semantic relationships, entity coverage, and content structure rather than just keyword density. The scores reliably correlate with ranking potential when combined with other SEO best practices.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I use Neuron Writer for multiple languages?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Neuron Writer supports 80+ languages with location-specific SERP analysis. You can optimize content for different countries and languages using their respective search results. This makes it excellent for international SEO and multi-market content strategies.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What's included in the Bronze plan?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">The Bronze plan ($23/month) includes 25 content analyses per month, basic NLP optimization, SERP analysis, content planning tools, and keyword research. It's perfect for solo content creators or small blogs who need professional optimization on a budget. You can always upgrade as your needs grow.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Is there a free trial available?<span>+</span></div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Neuron Writer offers a 3-day free trial that gives you full access to all features including NLP optimization, SERP analysis, and content planning. While 3 days is shorter than some competitors, it's enough to test the core functionality and determine if it fits your workflow.</div></div>
